  "faqMyDayQ": "What does “Start my day” do?",
  "faqMyDayA": "Once a day the home screen offers it: see today’s tasks, the next event, habits left and cards due, then begin a focus session with one tap. Long-press the app icon for quick actions, or add the home screen widget to see focus time and cards due.",
  "faqTasksQ": "How do I add a task with a reminder?",
  "faqTasksA": "Tap New task on Home or + in Tasks. Type the title or speak it with the microphone, then set a due date, a time and a reminder. Overdue tasks are listed first.",
  "faqFocusQ": "How does the focus timer work?",
  "faqFocusA": "Choose Pomodoro, a countdown or open time and press Start; breaks can follow automatically. In Settings you can pick the end sound, turn on Do Not Disturb while focusing, and play your nature sounds with each session.",
  "faqSoundsQ": "Can I mix nature sounds?",
  "faqSoundsA": "Turn on up to six real recordings, set each volume and save the mix by name. They keep playing in the background, and a sleep timer can stop them. No music is used.",
  "faqCalendarQ": "Can the calendar show Hijri dates?",
  "faqCalendarA": "Yes. Hijri dates (Umm al-Qura) show automatically in Arabic and can be turned on in Settings for any language. Events, tasks with due dates and project milestones appear together.",
  "faqFlashcardsQ": "How does review decide which cards I see?",
  "faqFlashcardsA": "Cards you know well come back after longer gaps and cards you miss come back soon (spaced repetition). Rate each answer Again, Hard, Good or Easy. Set a daily goal and keep your streak on the Today card. Set an exam date in a deck to see the days left and how many new cards to learn each day. Sort by \"My order\" to drag cards into place, tap the speaker on either side to hear it, and set speed and repeats in the Speech menu.",
  "faqImportQ": "Can I bring cards from Anki or Excel?",
  "faqImportA": "Yes. In a deck choose Import, then pick a file: Anki (.apkg), Excel (.xlsx) or CSV, and match the columns. Use “Spreadsheet template” to write cards on a computer. Pictures and sounds inside Anki files are not imported.",
  "faqNotesQ": "What can notes do?",
  "faqNotesA": "Write freely with checklists and formatting, pin or favourite important notes, add tags and link notes to tasks. The microphone button lets you dictate. A new note can start from a template (lecture, book summary, journal, weekly plan), and the picture button adds photos.",
  "faqHabitsQ": "How are habit streaks counted?",
  "faqHabitsA": "A day counts when you reach the habit’s target on a scheduled day. Pausing a habit keeps the streak safe. Each habit can have its own reminder time.",
  "faqGoalsQ": "How do goals track progress?",
  "faqGoalsA": "Give a goal a target amount and unit, then log progress. Its card shows how far you are and how much is left before the deadline.",
  "faqProjectsQ": "What are projects for?",
  "faqProjectsA": "Group tasks under a project, add milestones with dates and follow overall progress. Milestones also appear in the calendar.",
  "faqInsightsQ": "What does Insights show?",
  "faqInsightsA": "Your focus time, finished tasks and study over days and weeks, with gentle suggestions. Everything is calculated on your phone.",
  "faqSpacesQ": "Where are all the sections?",
  "faqSpacesA": "Spaces lists every part of the app (notes, decks, habits, goals, projects, sounds and more) so the main bar stays simple.",
  "faqBackupQ": "How are my data backed up?",
  "faqBackupA": "Every day the app quietly keeps an encrypted copy on this phone and keeps the last 7. In Settings you can also export a password-protected backup file and restore it on another phone.",
  "faqPrayerQ": "How do prayer times work?",
  "faqPrayerA": "Choose your city in Settings → Prayer times. Times are calculated on the phone with the method used there, and you can change the method and the Asr school. You can be notified at each prayer, and a running focus session pauses.",
  "faqPrivacyQ": "Where are my data stored?",
  "faqPrivacyA": "On your phone only, in an encrypted database. There is no account and no tracking. The internet is used only by features you turn on yourself, such as the optional assistant.",
  "faqAssistantQ": "What is the assistant?",
  "faqAssistantA": "An optional helper you connect to your own AI service in Settings. It is off by default and asks before sending any note text.",
  "tourPlanTitle": "Plan your day",
  "tourPlanBody": "Tasks, calendar and habits in one calm place. Begin each morning with “Start my day”.",
  "tourFocusTitle": "Focus deeply",
  "tourFocusBody": "Timed sessions with real nature sounds, Do Not Disturb and gentle end tones.",
  "tourLearnTitle": "Learn for good",
  "tourLearnBody": "Flashcards with spaced repetition, speech in many languages, and imports from Anki or Excel.",
